<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gassantoda Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gassan-Toda Castle, Gassan Toda Castle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gassantoda Castle was a mountain castle at Hirose in Izumo province, now part of Yasugi in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimane-prefecture">Shimane Prefecture</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. As the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amago-clan">Amago clan</a> it withstood a siege by the Ōuchi in 1542–1543 but fell to Mōri Motonari in 1566 after a long siege. It was abandoned in the early 17th century when the lords of Izumo moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsue">Matsue</a>, and only earthworks and stone walls remain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gassantoda-castle.jpg" alt="Gassantoda Castle" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 安来市政策秘書課 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9C%88%E5%B1%B1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
